        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): admit plugin HTTP work during suspension",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCloses #104077.\n\nCooperative suspension could report the Gateway ready while an ordinary plugin HTTP handler or plugin-owned WebSocket upgrade was still deciding ownership. New plugin work could also begin after the root-work fence closed, allowing a host to stop during untracked network or state side effects.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Move the canonical HTTP rejection and admission logic into a small Gateway boundary module shared by core and plugin routes.\n- Acquire root admission only after plugin route matching and authentication, preserving exact/prefix fallthrough and avoiding false `503` responses for unmatched requests.\n- Hold admission through each ordinary handler or upgrade ownership decision and release it on success, fallthrough, or error.\n- Preserve the manifest-derived `gatewayMethodDispatch` entitlement for trusted control-plane HTTP routes. These routes may do bounded validation/discovery, but substantive work delegates through Gateway method dispatch so `gateway.suspend.prepare` remains a true root request.\n- Keep established plugin WebSocket lifetime outside this patch; this change covers only the atomic upgrade ownership boundary.\n\n## User Impact\n\nHosts can now rely on ordinary plugin HTTP handlers and new plugin WebSocket upgrades when evaluating suspension readiness. While prepared, those paths receive the same `503` boundary response as built-in HTTP work, while authenticated Admin HTTP suspension status and resume remain reachable.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kx7fqgk4tjw6e9zw6dar21gs`: focused Gateway, plugin-route, preauth, and Admin HTTP suite — 215 tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox: full `pnpm build` passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox: `docs:list`, MDX, link, i18n-glossary, and docs-format checks passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox: path-scoped `pnpm check:changed` passed after rebasing onto current `main`.\n- `git diff --check` and targeted oxfmt passed.\n- Fresh autoreview completed with no accepted/actionable findings after correcting the bounded `commands.list` documentation.\n\nAI-assisted implementation; maintainer-reviewed against current `main`. No agent transcript is included.\n",
